=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is completely healthy and the helpdesk ticket is based on a false premise. Direct probing of every device in the dc_clos_bgp fabric shows that leaf_router_0_1's two spine-facing uplinks — eth0 (172.16.0.7/31, toward spine_router_0_0) and eth1 (172.16.0.11/31, toward spine_router_0_1) — are both in UP/LOWER_UP state with active traffic counters and correctly assigned IP addresses. No interface anywhere in the fabric is down or in a degraded state. The BGP routing plane is fully converged: leaf_router_0_1 holds a valid BGP route to 10.0.0.0/24 via spine_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_0 holds a valid BGP route to 10.0.1.0/24 via spine_router_0_0, and super_spine_router_0 carries BGP-learned routes to both leaf subnets. End-to-end verification — a live ping from pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) to pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) — returns all four packets with 0% loss and sub-2 ms RTT. The team's assertion that "both spine-facing links on leaf_router_0_1 are down" is factually incorrect; no such outage exists now or appears to have occurred. The reported connectivity complaint is not reproducible, and no corrective action is warranted on any device or link.
=== END ===